# Write down the relationship

A resistor model relates the voltage across the component to the current through it. Use consistent reference directions when writing the relationship.

## A simple example

Two equal resistors in series carry the same current. Their voltage drops add to the total applied voltage.

**Useful relationship:** R total = R₁ + R₂

## Pause and try

Sketch two resistors in series. Mark a current direction and each voltage drop.

